        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "feat(android): add licenses settings screen",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAndroid users did not have an in-app place to inspect bundled third-party/open-source license notices from Settings, and maintainers did not have scoped Android agent guidance for keeping that surface current when dependencies change.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis adds a Settings-tab Licenses section backed by packaged UTF-8 `.txt` assets. The screen discovers license files at runtime, sorts rows by display title, renders detail text in monospace, and documents the maintenance contract in `apps/android/AGENTS.md`. It also removes obsolete Android audio SDK guards that were no longer needed with the app's current minimum SDK.\n\n## User Impact\n\nAndroid users can open Settings, tap Licenses, and read bundled third-party license notices without leaving the app. Maintainers can add or update license notice files on disk without hardcoding new rows in application source.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `pnpm docs:list`\n- `git diff --check`\n- `./gradlew :app:assemblePlayDebug --console=plain`\n- `.agents/skills/autoreview/scripts/autoreview --mode branch --base origin/main`\n- Live emulator screenshot proof generated locally under `.artifacts/android-licenses-e2e/final-current/`:\n  - `02-settings-licenses-row.png`\n  - `03-licenses-list.png`\n  - `04-license-detail.png`\n",
